What are Hydraulic Stack Valves?
Hydraulic Stack Valves represent a sophisticated category of fluid power components that enable modular hydraulic circuit design through their unique superposition capability. These multi-functional valves serve dual purposes as both control elements and integrated flow passages, eliminating intermediate piping through direct stacking of multiple valve sections. Their compact architecture provides significant advantages over conventional hydraulic valves by reducing system footprint while improving reliability through minimized connection points. This technology finds extensive application across construction equipment, industrial machinery, and agricultural systems where precise control of fluid pressure, direction and flow is paramount.
